// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5676 add detection rule for suspicious use of BrowserCore.exe in PRT extra…
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5676
// Pull request author: e0909
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Use of BrowserCore.exe for PRT Extraction
// Sigma ID: e862850e-cf85-48eb-b47b-db55d5c3d2d6
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Eugen Tropmann
// Date: 2026-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1539, T1555.003
// Description: Detects suspicious execution of BrowserCore.exe potentially used to extract Primary Refresh
//   Tokens (PRTs) for Azure AD SSO abuse. Legitimate executions are typically spawned by a browser
//   (like Chrome or Edge) via cmd.exe using named pipes for inter-process communication. An attacker
//   can execute BrowserCore.exe directly to request a Primary Refresh Token (PRT) cookie as part of
//   an Azure AD SSO abuse attack.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://dirkjanm.io/abusing-azure-ad-sso-with-the-primary-refresh-token/
//   - https://falconforce.nl/falconfriday-stealing-and-detecting-azure-prt-cookies-0xff18/
//   - https://specterops.io/blog/2020/07/14/requesting-azure-ad-request-tokens-on-azure-ad-joined-machines-for-browser-sso/
//   - https://aadinternals.com/post/prt/
//   - https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/windows/credential_access_entraid_prt_via_browsercore/
//   - https://github.com/dirkjanm/ROADtoken/tree/48f75b691a4f7fa9ab7606ec592531c5952f52ed
//   - https://github.com/kozmer/aad-bofs/tree/6f03d71fd8f6633c7266fa24bc196efe900e5f31/request_aad_prt
//   - https://github.com/leechristensen/RequestAADRefreshToken/tree/5b8d5390ea190242b5fafb6f24b28b83b8b1b57c
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/devices/concept-primary-refresh-token
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/28de4dd8e97659c6e32258dee20172ade1d9352a/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_prt_attack_browsercore.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\BrowserCore.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "BrowserCore.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "chrome-extension://ppnbnpeolgkicgegkbkbjmhlideopiji/") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "\\.\\pipe\\")))
